Description: gpio: add the i.MX21 keypad port as GPIO
 Boards such as the Chumby Classic don't wire a key matrix to the
 i.MX21 keypad port: its columns switch power rails and its rows read
 buttons. With KPCR cleared, KDDR and KPDR are a plain 16-bit GPIO port,
 so drive it with gpio-generic: rows are lines 0-7, columns lines 8-15.
 The port can't interrupt on a single row, so there are no interrupts.
